### College Event Management System - Backend API Tests

### 1. Register New Student
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "John Doe",
  "studentId": "STU001",
  "email": "john@student.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "role": "STUDENT"
}

### 2. Register New Admin
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Admin User",
  "studentId": "ADMIN001",
  "email": "admin@college.edu",
  "password": "admin123",
  "role": "ADMIN"
}

### 3. Login as Student
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john@student.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 4. Login as Admin
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@college.edu",
  "password": "admin123"
}

### 5. Get All Published Events (Public)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/events

### 6. Create Event (Admin Only) - Replace YOUR_ADMIN_TOKEN
POST http://localhost:8080/api/events
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ADMIN_TOKEN
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Tech Symposium 2024",
  "description": "Annual technology symposium featuring latest innovations",
  "eventDate": "2024-12-25",
  "startTime": "09:00",
  "endTime": "17:00",
  "location": "Main Auditorium",
  "maxCapacity": 200,
  "status": "PUBLISHED"
}

### 7. Create Draft Event (Admin Only) - Replace YOUR_ADMIN_TOKEN
POST http://localhost:8080/api/events
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ADMIN_TOKEN
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Cultural Fest 2024",
  "description": "Annual cultural festival with music and dance",
  "eventDate": "2024-12-30",
  "startTime": "18:00",
  "endTime": "22:00",
  "location": "College Ground",
  "maxCapacity": 500,
  "status": "DRAFT"
}

### 8. Get All Events for Admin - Replace YOUR_ADMIN_TOKEN
GET http://localhost:8080/api/events/admin/all
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ADMIN_TOKEN

### 9. Get Specific Event Details - Replace EVENT_ID
GET http://localhost:8080/api/events/1

### 10. Update Event (Admin Only) - Replace YOUR_ADMIN_TOKEN and EVENT_ID
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/events/1
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ADMIN_TOKEN
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Updated Tech Symposium 2024",
  "description": "Updated description for technology symposium",
  "eventDate": "2024-12-26",
  "startTime": "10:00",
  "endTime": "16:00",
  "location": "Updated Auditorium",
  "maxCapacity": 250,
  "status": "PUBLISHED"
}

### 11. Register for Event (Student Only) - Replace YOUR_STUDENT_TOKEN and EVENT_ID
POST http://localhost:8080/api/events/1/register
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_STUDENT_TOKEN

### 12. Get User's Registered Events - Replace YOUR_STUDENT_TOKEN and USER_ID
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/2/events
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_STUDENT_TOKEN

### 13. Get Event Registrations (Admin Only) - Replace YOUR_ADMIN_TOKEN and EVENT_ID
GET http://localhost:8080/api/events/1/registrations
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ADMIN_TOKEN

### 14. Delete Event (Admin Only) - Replace YOUR_ADMIN_TOKEN and EVENT_ID
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/events/2
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ADMIN_TOKEN

### Test Invalid Scenarios

### 15. Try to Create Event as Student (Should Fail)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/events
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_STUDENT_TOKEN
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Unauthorized Event",
  "description": "This should fail",
  "eventDate": "2024-12-25",
  "startTime": "09:00",
  "endTime": "17:00",
  "location": "Test Hall",
  "maxCapacity": 100,
  "status": "PUBLISHED"
}

### 16. Try to Register with Duplicate Email (Should Fail)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Duplicate User",
  "studentId": "STU002",
  "email": "john@student.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "role": "STUDENT"
}

### 17. Try to Login with Wrong Credentials (Should Fail)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john@student.com",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}

### Instructions:
# 1. Start your backend server: mvn spring-boot:run
# 2. Run tests 1-4 first to get tokens
# 3. Copy the tokens from login responses
# 4. Replace YOUR_ADMIN_TOKEN and YOUR_STUDENT_TOKEN in subsequent requests
# 5. Replace EVENT_ID and USER_ID with actual IDs from responses
# 6. Run tests in order for best results